  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to early recovery in war-affected areas in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Support to early recovery in war-affected areas in Ukraine - As Ukrainian forces liberate parts of Ukraine from Russian military control, Ukrainian authorities and communities are faced with immense recovery needs that need to be urgently addressed in order to reestablish public services, relaunch social and economic activities and provide support to local populations. Ukraine&#xbf;s economy has been very seriously affected by the war. The combination of infrastructure damage, exodus of the population and interrupted transport links have resulted in a halving of economic activity compared to pre-war levels. At the same time government spending for social and military expenditure has sharply increased. To face these unprecedented challenges, Ukraine&#xbf;s government is dependent on external support. In response to the massive destruction in multiple locations in Ukraine, this 18-month measure will provide immediate practical support to Ukrainian authorities to address environmental and public health threats in post-combat localities and territories liberated from Russian military control. This will entail, but will not be limited to, support to debris removal, removal of hazardous waste and materials from damaged industrial facilities and critical infrastructure, and re-establishment of water and electricity supply.</narrative>
  </description>
